      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Lack of Specialized Medical Decoys: Most existing honeypot frameworks (like Cowrie or T-Pot) focus on general IT protocols (SSH, Telnet) or Industrial systems (SCADA). There is a critical shortage of lightweight honeypots specifically emulating IoMT (Internet of Medical Things) protocols like HL7, DICOM, and medical web portals.\n\nOver-reliance on Static, Outdated Datasets: Many machine learning intrusion detection systems (IDS) are trained on old, static datasets (like NSL-KDD) that do not reflect modern IoT/IoMT attack vectors. Furthermore, they are rarely validated against live traffic generated on edge hardware.\n\nCloud-Dependency and Latency: Current threat intelligence models often send raw data to the cloud for analysis, which introduces latency and privacy risks for healthcare networks. There is a gap in deploying the ML inference engine directly on the edge device (Raspberry Pi) for zero-latency detection.",
